1
00:00:01,286 --> 00:00:04,363
Every night, Indian Railways runs thousands of trains.

2
00:00:04,363 --> 00:00:10,347
When something goes wrong, the evidence is scattered across radio recordings, cab videos and wagon scans.

3
00:00:10,347 --> 00:00:12,968
An inquiry costs officers days of manual work.

4
00:00:13,399 --> 00:00:15,731
AiSPRY already captures that evidence.

5
00:00:15,731 --> 00:00:17,756
Railcomm cleans noisy loco radio.

6
00:00:17,756 --> 00:00:20,579
Locate spots phone use and fatigue in the cab.

7
00:00:20,579 --> 00:00:24,384
Wagon Damage Detection compares every wagon at entry and exit.

8
00:00:25,382 --> 00:00:27,475
RailKavach Copilot brings all three together.

9
00:00:27,475 --> 00:00:31,103
Each officer signs in by role, and sees only what that role is allowed to see.

10
00:00:31,514 --> 00:00:36,602
The safety officer sees the whole night shift on one screen, and every number traces back to a record.

11
00:00:36,959 --> 00:00:41,112
Now, one question about train 12414 near Suratgarh.

12
00:00:41,463 --> 00:00:48,734
In seconds, it lines up the station master's call, the assistant pilot's warning and the emergency brake, and gives a clear verdict.

13
00:00:48,734 --> 00:00:50,166
The signal was not passed.

14
00:00:50,623 --> 00:00:52,865
Every claim is tied to its original file.

15
00:00:52,865 --> 00:00:59,317
One click re-checks the file's digital fingerprint, so the evidence holds up under Section 63 of the new Evidence Act.

16
00:00:59,773 --> 00:01:01,777
Officers can also just speak.

17
00:01:01,777 --> 00:01:03,712
Hindi, English, or Hinglish.

18
00:01:04,963 --> 00:01:11,992
[Officer] “Rake BOXN-542 mein kitne wagons damaged hain, aur kaun sa wagon critical hai?”

19
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,119
It replies in the same language, with exact counts, and reads the answer aloud in Indian English.

20
00:01:21,587 --> 00:01:23,548
Privacy is enforced on the server.

21
00:01:23,548 --> 00:01:26,373
A crew controller asking about wagons is refused.

22
00:01:26,373 --> 00:01:31,851
Identities stay masked under the DPDP Act, and every request lands in a tamper-proof audit log.

23
00:01:32,802 --> 00:01:33,448
The result.

24
00:01:33,448 --> 00:01:35,914
Inquiries that took days now take minutes.

25
00:01:35,914 --> 00:01:38,145
Decisions rest on verifiable evidence.

26
00:01:38,145 --> 00:01:42,900
And it runs on Google Cloud with Gemini, or fully on railway premises with Gemma.

27
00:01:43,319 --> 00:01:45,866
RailKavach Copilot, by AiSPRY.

28
00:01:45,866 --> 00:01:46,630
Ask once.

29
00:01:46,630 --> 00:01:48,073
Get the evidence.
